<item><title>Namibia starts second FMD vaccination round in //Kharas</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-starts-second-fmd-vaccination-round-in-kharas-8bedd8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-starts-second-fmd-vaccination-round-in-kharas-8bedd8/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>Veterinary teams began the campaign on 16 November, as the outbreak remained at 131 confirmed cases across 18 farms.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:08:20 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Koryx values Namibia’s Haib copper project at US$2.5 billion</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/koryx-values-namibia-s-haib-copper-project-at-us-2-5-billion-f2fc97/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/koryx-values-namibia-s-haib-copper-project-at-us-2-5-billion-f2fc97/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>The pre-feasibility study projects 130 000 tonnes of payable copper a year in the mine’s first 10 years and targets early construction works in 2027.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:14:57 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Namibia tracks 71% of Sustainable Development Goal indicators</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-tracks-71-of-sustainable-development-goal-indicators-d5d284/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-tracks-71-of-sustainable-development-goal-indicators-d5d284/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>The statistics agency’s 2025 framework covers 176 of 248 measures, up from 66.4% in 2019, but leaves gaps in three goals.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:02:15 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" length="33196" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/na.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Namibia seeks US$12.6 billion in international climate funding by 2035</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-seeks-us-12-6-billion-in-international-climate-60a5eb/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-seeks-us-12-6-billion-in-international-climate-60a5eb/</guid><category>Namibia</category><description>National planning chief Kaire Mbuende says the country needs US$14 billion to meet its climate commitments and cut emissions.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:00:23 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-seeks-us-12-6-billion-in-international-climate-60a5eb/share.jpg" length="45338" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/na/namibia-seeks-us-12-6-billion-in-international-climate-60a5eb/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
